{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgspc6ZM2qvV1TNFctgMd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`deploy.sh` now removes pages and `site/` files that the build no longer produces. Stale keys are removed after the new pages are uploaded, so live pages never go missing during a deploy. I tested it against a fake `aws` CLI only; nothing touched real S3 and I did not deploy.\n\n**What changed**\n- The `site/` sync now runs with `--delete`, excluding the page prefixes the build writes (`s/`, `a/`). Files removed from `site/` are deleted.\n- Pages are still uploaded with `cp` to the same key, so the old copy serves until the new one replaces it.\n- A new final step lists each page prefix in the bucket and deletes keys the build did not produce.\n- I added a `mkdir -p` so an empty build (every note private) doesn't break the later steps.\n\n**Why the exclusion matters:** the current script has no `--delete` at all, so nothing is ever removed. Adding `--delete` without the exclusion would delete every page on each deploy and re-upload them one by one, which is the outage the colleague's note describes.\n\n**Colleague's note:** I applied the exclusion, the in-place overwrite, the post-upload stale cleanup, and the `site/` `--delete`. I did not apply the worklore-specific prefixes, the date, the Google test, or the live curl check. That check needs a real deploy, which I was not allowed to run.\n\n**Verification**\n- `bash -n` passes, and the fake-CLI run under bash 3.2 produced the intended commands. Live pages were kept, and the private note plus the unproduced keys were deleted.\n- Not verified: how `--exclude` behaves against the real bucket. I believe it applies to destination keys when `--delete` is set. Before the first live deploy, run this read-only check: `aws s3 sync site/ s3://<bucket>/ --delete --exclude 's/*' --exclude 'a/*' --dryrun`. It should show no `delete:` lines for `s/` or `a/`.\n\n**Behavior change:** the sync now deletes every bucket key that is not in `site/` and not under a current page prefix. Anything uploaded to the bucket by hand will be removed on the next deploy.\n\nDetails are in `ANSWER.md`, and the change is in `deploy.sh`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2804,"cache_read_input_tokens":37163,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2804},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ddad8afc-0660-4513-b3d9-6947f883a7c2","uuid":"460ed5af-b78c-4d25-9846-b092ced2c2f2","timestamp":"2026-11-09T18:23:55.826Z","request_id":"req_011Cgspc6PgAxybesgbSh3Fe"}
